    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T10:32:43Z",
    "body": "Maintainer decision (owner's standing word 2026-11-22: choose recommended while he sleeps): this issue is `P3`, not `P1`.\n\n- The coordinator set `P1` on the condition of a plunge with the full tool disc in uncut stock. After PR #3684 no such plunge remains. The open case is an 18 mm plunge beside a 2.5 mm crescent of uncut sheet.\n- Nothing gouges or collides, and the posted part geometry is correct. The risk is the tool load. The verifier has no law for plunge depth: this is a missing check, not a check that passes wrongly.\n- The generator defect is #3678 (`P3`). A workaround exists: no lead-in makes each dive 2.7 mm.\n\nOptions: (a) `P3` (taken); (b) keep `P1` (dropped: the `P1` row is for a gouge, a collision or wrong posted G-code that passes).\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
